hi I'm Eve aka madam Medtronic as the  all new national living statue  championship is coming up this April  I've made a video of my top five living  statue tips alongside one of my makeup  routines  tip one look after your skin a lot of  face paint can be harsh on your skin so  it is a good idea to moisturize before  and after a show I always use coconut  oil or Vaseline to act as a slight  barrier under the makeup I also  personally find that removing face paint  with soap and hot water rather than  makeup wipes is better for your skin in  the long run tip to get comfy okay maybe  not that comfy you're likely to be  standing in the same pose for long  periods of time so you want to make sure  it's a comfortable one try not to tense  your muscles too much as this leads to  uncontrolled shaking and often cramp  also I'd avoid holding your arms above  shoulder level for too long as blood  circulation becomes more difficult tip 3  good coverage now this might sound  obvious but as you can see in the video  it's really important to cover every  tiny bit of skin that might be on show  because trust me is quite obvious in  daylight and the audience members do  come up and check  tip for don't get dizzy standing for  long periods of time can lower your  blood pressure and blood sugar levels to  prevent possible dizzy spells it's  important to make sure you keep hydrated  and eat well it also helps to maintain a  good body temperature which leads me to  tip fights prepare for all weathers now  this is England it's often cold and it  rains a lot  so waterproofing your costumes are  making sure you can fit lots of layers  underneath is really useful you'll be  surprised at how cold you can get when  you can't move to keep warm equally for  those precious hot days having a cooler  more breathable costume and trying to  keep out of direct sunlight for long  periods of time can help with  overheating  okay so I've been mother Medtronic I  hope you've enjoyed my top tips you can  find out more about me on Facebook  Twitter and Instagram or better yet you  could come and find me at the national  living statues championships in April in  stratford-upon-avon
 

